<DocsLayout
  title="Getting Started with the Python openEHR SDK | oehrpy"
  description="Documentation for oehrpy, the Python openEHR SDK: install it with pip, create your first Reference Model objects, and find guides for templates, FLAT and canonical JSON, the EHRBase client, AQL and validation."
  path="docs.html"
  heading="Getting Started with oehrpy"
>
  <p class="lead">oehrpy is a Python SDK for <a href="https://openehr.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">openEHR</a>, the open standard for vendor-neutral electronic health records. It gives you type-safe Reference Model classes, template-based composition builders, canonical JSON and FLAT serialization, an async EHRBase client and an AQL query builder. New to openEHR? The <a href="/workflow.html">openEHR workflow overview</a> explains how templates, compositions and CDRs fit together.</p>

  <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
  <p>Install oehrpy using pip:</p>
  <pre><code>pip install oehrpy</code></pre>

  <p>Or install from source for development:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/platzhersh/oehrpy.git
cd oehrpy
pip install -e ".[dev]"</code></pre>

  <div class="note">
    <p><strong>Requirements:</strong> Python 3.10 or higher is required.</p>
  </div>
  <h2 id="quick-start">Quick Start</h2>
  <p>Here's a quick example to get you started with oehrpy:</p>
  <pre><code><span class="keyword">from</span> oehrpy.rm <span class="keyword">import</span> DV_TEXT, DV_QUANTITY, CODE_PHRASE, TERMINOLOGY_ID

<span class="comment"># Create a simple text value</span>
text = DV_TEXT(value=<span class="string">"Patient temperature recorded"</span>)

<span class="comment"># Create a quantity with units</span>
temperature = DV_QUANTITY(
    magnitude=<span class="string">37.2</span>,
    units=<span class="string">"°C"</span>,
    property=CODE_PHRASE(
        terminology_id=TERMINOLOGY_ID(value=<span class="string">"openehr"</span>),
        code_string=<span class="string">"127"</span>
    )
)

<span class="keyword">print</span>(<span class="string">f"Temperature: &#123;temperature.magnitude&#125; &#123;temperature.units&#125;"</span>)</code></pre>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>oehrpy is a comprehensive Python SDK for openEHR that provides:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/reference-model.html">Type-safe RM Classes</a>:</strong> 134 Pydantic models for openEHR Reference Model 1.1.0 (includes BASE types)</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/templates.html#opt-parser">OPT Parser &amp; Code Generation</a>:</strong> Parse OPT 1.4 XML files and auto-generate type-safe Python builder classes</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/templates.html#template-builders">Template Builders</a>:</strong> Pre-built composition builders for common clinical templates</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/serialization.html#flat-format">FLAT Format Support</a>:</strong> Full support for EHRBase FLAT format serialization</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/serialization.html#canonical-json">Canonical JSON</a>:</strong> Convert between RM objects and openEHR canonical JSON</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/ehrbase-client.html">EHRBase Client</a>:</strong> Async REST client for EHRBase CDR operations</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/aql.html">AQL Builder</a>:</strong> Fluent API for building type-safe AQL queries</li>
    <li><strong><a href="/docs/reference-model.html#type-safety">Full IDE Support</a>:</strong> Complete autocomplete and type checking</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="guides">Guides</h2>
  <ul class="docs-guides">
    <li><a href="/docs/reference-model.html">Reference Model</a>: the RM 1.1.0 classes, data types, validation and type safety</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/templates.html">Templates &amp; Builders</a>: parse OPT templates and build compositions</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/serialization.html">Serialization</a>: canonical JSON and the FLAT format</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/ehrbase-client.html">EHRBase Client</a>: EHRs, compositions and queries against EHRBase</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/aql.html">AQL Query Builder</a>: build AQL queries without string concatenation</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/validation.html">FLAT &amp; OPT Validation</a>: catch template mismatches before the CDR does</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/development.html">Development</a>: set up, regenerate the RM classes, run the tests</li>
  </ul>

